<p>CW/TW: Discussion of trans trauma, dysphoria, and suicide, by a trans individual.</p>
<p><a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/oystershell">http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/oystershell</a> Look under the &quot;<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Dysphoric Flesh</span>&quot; <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">&quot;Brood of my Brood, Skin of my Skin&quot;</span> &quot;Usurper&quot; tab.</p>
<p>This is a story about what truly horrifies me most. In case it's not clear, I'm trans myself.</p>
<p>While anyone and everyone's thoughts and critiques are welcome, I am especially keen on receiving feedback from other trans and non-binary folks.</p>
<p>EDIT 1: Draft 2 is now up. Draft 2 contains revised ConProcs, a slew of small edits and revisions to the Description including addressing almost all of cybersqyd's LBL's, and the addition of a reproductive system for the SCP. Still looking for feedback on sensitivity, as well as critique on the overall narrative and flow, as well as advice on how to stick the landing if the current ending is underwhelming for you. Also added an image and revised the title.</p>
<p>EDIT 2: I've created an alternate version, Available under the &quot;Their Eyes Don't Cry&quot; tab. I've cut down the description to just the bare minimum, and have finished the article off with two case files in order to provide more of the human element. Even with the cuts, it's more than twice as long as &quot;Brood of my Brood&quot; and I'm quite unsure about parts of it. Regardless, please let me know which version you prefer and which should get my attention as I continue to revise.</p>
<p>EDIT 3: After some careful consideration, I've decided to go with the long ending, but I've cut it and re-written it entirely. It's shorter now and I'm happier with the quality. Let me know what you think.</p>
<p>Thanks in advance.</p>

