<p>Summoned by PM</p>
<p>I'm not going to do an LBL on this just now because I have a queue to get through - if you'd like one let me know and I can try and do one next week.</p>
<p>I enjoyed this. There is a really&#8230; uncomfortable sense to the progression here. On some level, I feel genuinely a little gross about reading the story of this person's suffering, knowing what will happen the whole way through, and just having it happen without being able to do anything about it. That being said, it's the kind of uncomfortable and gross that works, I think, largely because of the fact that it's clearly framed as such.</p>
<p>I've considered saying that the ending is a little flat, but I don't think there's a solid way to change that which wouldn't also make the article overall feel just a bit <em>too</em> uncomfortable? I'm not entirely sure, to be honest. The ending is a little less climactic than it could be, I think, but it's not bad. Like <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/warfang" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2112729); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2112729&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608842206" alt="WarFang" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2112729)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/warfang" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2112729); return false;">WarFang</a></span> said, it's a relief to see Lief is okay, and that might be enough on its own.</p>
<p>I think the voice constructed for Lief could be a little more&#8230; distinct? It's not bad, but it doesn't feel particularly unique and given the emotional and narrative core of the article is built around those diary entries, and therefore Lief's voice, it could do with being a bit more compelling in my opinion. Give the reader more to latch onto, and it will make the overall arc even more involving and engaging.</p>
<p>Otherwise, I think this is a solid piece of writing. Well done, and I wish you the best of luck with it.</p>

